# Subtest: virgin seed fixture binds startup admission and storage to one unique owned directory
    ok 1 - concurrent virgin seeds never share implicit physical storage
    ok 2 - startup admission and storage manager use the same canonical path
    ok 3 - each concurrent fixture retains its own canonical path
    ok 4 - both owned directories exist before shutdown
    ok 5 - first owned directory is removed on shutdown
    ok 6 - second owned directory is removed on shutdown
    1..6
ok 2 - virgin seed fixture binds startup admission and storage to one unique owned directory # time=58.061ms

# Subtest: virgin seed fixture preserves startup-owner identity and explicit authority choices
    ok 1 - should be equal
    ok 2 - absent authority uses the actual startup decision owner
    ok 3 - derived fresh-seed authority is accepted
    ok 4 - the actual owner validates its exact participant/build token
    ok 5 - an explicit canonical owner outcome retains object identity
    ok 6 - the actual owner accepts the explicit canonical outcome
    ok 7 - explicit null is not replaced by derived authority
    ok 8 - the actual owner refuses explicit null
    ok 9 - the unchanged constructor canonically stores explicit undefined as null
    ok 10 - the actual owner refuses explicit undefined
    ok 11 - an explicit invalid outcome retains object identity
    ok 12 - the actual owner refuses the explicit invalid outcome
    ok 13 - an inherited outcome is absent and actual authority is derived
    ok 14 - an inherited outcome is absent and actual derived authority is accepted
    ok 15 - node ID is captured before the first helper await
    ok 16 - node address is captured before the first helper await
    ok 17 - the captured identity keeps the selected directory
    ok 18 - later option mutation cannot replace the captured absent-owner decision
    ok 19 - own-present node ID is captured before the first helper await
    ok 20 - own-present node address is captured before the first helper await
    ok 21 - own-present authority retains its exact captured pre-await value
    ok 22 - the actual owner refuses the captured value after caller replacement
    ok 23 - shutdown leaves every caller-owned directory with the caller
    1..23
ok 3 - virgin seed fixture preserves startup-owner identity and explicit authority choices # time=43.278ms

# Subtest: joining-node fixture owns unique stable paths across retries
    ok 1 - a retry for one logical node reuses its exact storage identity
    ok 2 - different logical nodes receive distinct canonical paths
    ok 3 - an explicit dataDir remains authoritative
    ok 4 - a virgin logical node receives canonical initial boot identity
    ok 5 - a new boot lifecycle for the same node reserves a strictly larger incarnation
    ok 6 - an explicit boot identity remains authoritative
    ok 7 - the fixture proves path uniqueness before join begins
    ok 8 - the owned retry directory exists before shutdown
    ok 9 - ending one attempt does not destroy storage needed by its retry
    ok 10 - final owner shutdown removes implicitly owned storage
    ok 11 - final owner shutdown does not remove caller-owned explicit storage
    1..11
ok 4 - joining-node fixture owns unique stable paths across retries # time=35.635ms

